<</A<</BBox[53.9717 418.224 557.972 707.981]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>/Alt(Distribution of precursors and co-reactants used in ZnO and IGZO literature shown as number of studies. \(a\) And \(b\) summarize the zinc precursors and co-reactants used for ZnO ALD, respectively, highlighting the strong dominance of DEZn with H2O as the primary co-reactant. \(c\) And \(d\) show the corresponding precursor and co-reactant distributions for IGZO ALD and more specifically at the sub-oxide level for In2O3, Ga2O3 and ZnO. IGZO data reveal a greater diversity of chemistries compared to ZnO, relying on O2 plasma as the co-reactant. Chemical species were normalized during the extraction workflow, with the corresponding PubChem CIDs provided in the supplementary material.)/K 29/Lang(en-EN)/P 34 0 R/Pg 206 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
